\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Let $r(C_m,K_n)$ be the least number of vertices that forces a red cycle of length $m$ or a blue clique of size $n$ in every red-blue edge-coloring of a complete graph. Is
\[r(C_m,K_n)=(m-1)(n-1)+1\]
for all $m\geq n$?
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://www.overleaf.com/read/mnvcscjjysvg}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Let $r(C_m,K_n)$ be the least number of vertices that forces a red cycle of length $m$ or a blue clique of size $n$ in every red-blue edge-coloring of a complete graph. Is
\[r(C_m,K_n)=(m-1)(n-1)+1\]
for all $m\geq n$?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 20000946 (AIM-COMBINATORICS-0071). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://www.overleaf.com/read/mnvcscjjysvg}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:20000946}

